 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "s contains only ASCII letters. Build a tree whose leaves are the distinct characters (node {ch, count, left: null, right: null}) and whose internal nodes have ch '#' and count equal to the sum of their two children. The construction is inferred to be Huffman-style: start with the leaves ordered by character code, repeatedly merge the two lowest-count nodes (ties broken by creation order, leaves first by character code, merged nodes numbered afterwards in creation order), the first removed becoming the left child. Return the root, or null for an empty string.",
  "provenance": [
